# The set of checks clang-tidy runs.
#
# Checks are named explicitly so diagnostics stay limited to rules relevant to
# this project.
#
# tools/run-clang-tidy.py points at this file. It is the only thing that runs
# clang-tidy here; `pio check` covers cppcheck alone, for reasons that script
# explains.
#
# The selected groups focus on correctness, portability, and maintainability.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  concurrency-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-*,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters

# Why each of the above is off.
#
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-*
#   The bounds-safety profile of the C++ Core Guidelines. Satisfying it takes
#   gsl::span and gsl::at. GSL is not part of ESP-IDF and is not being added.
#   Fixed-size buffer indexing triggers these checks throughout the core.
#   Bounds are covered instead by focused overrun tests
#   (test_overflow_never_writes_past_the_buffer, in test_native_json_writer).
#
#   The whole family is named rather than its members. Two were listed
#   individually until clang-tidy 20 added a third,
#   pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access, which reported 112 findings for
#   the same reason the other two were already off -- so the list said nothing
#   about the position and only recorded which checks existed when it was
#   written.
#
# portability-avoid-pragma-once
#   Added in a later clang-tidy than the one CI pins. Every header here uses
#   `#pragma once`, which GCC, Clang and MSVC all support and the ESP-IDF
#   toolchain uses throughout its own headers. The check exists for toolchains
#   that do not, and this project does not build on one. Converting 66 headers
#   to include guards would be a large mechanical diff bought with nothing.
#
# misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes
#   CommandSpec and ParamSpec are intentional public data holders without
#   class invariants.
#
# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#   Some APIs intentionally accept adjacent values of one type, such as
#   member(key, value).

WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: 'stackchan/.*'
FormatStyle: file
